					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "DELAY\n\nThe Delay node allows you to delay a signal, event or attribute by a given amount of time (up to 20 seconds). By Default the Delay node will interpolate between frames to give you a smooth result. If you need to turn off interpolation for whatever reason, you do this by changing the Interpolate parameter in the node panel or by exposing the parameter (which is hidden by default).\n\nNote that the Texture2Drgba and Texture2Dchannel types will only be delayed by a single frame. If you want to delay textures for multiple frames you should use either the Ring Buffer or Buffer node."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 277.09625244140625,
					"width": 464.94073486328125,
					"x": -248.97088623046875,
					"y": -635.03173828125
				},
				"class": {
